# QA Activity Tracker — {{ project_name }}

`scripts/qa_track.py` records AI-assisted QA work per ticket, per sprint.

## Quick reference

```bash
# Open a record at the start of each ticket
python scripts/qa_track.py start \
  --ticket TICKET-1 \
  --title "My feature" \
  --sprint 26-01 \
  --basis ac \
  --activity qa,automation

# Close a record when the work is done
python scripts/qa_track.py basis --ticket TICKET-1 --basis both   # revise after the dossier
python scripts/qa_track.py count \
  --ticket TICKET-1 \
  --manual 5 \
  --automated 3 \
  --reason "2 cases need live auth unavailable in CI"

# Add a contextual note
python scripts/qa_track.py note --ticket TICKET-1 "Staging lag observed — waited 60s"

# Check which records are still missing counts
python scripts/qa_track.py status

# Generate the sprint report
python scripts/qa_track.py report --sprint 26-01
```

## Column semantics

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Ticket | The task key from {{ tracker_label }} |
| Title | The task's summary |
| QA | Resolved from `QA_NAME` env var or git `user.name` |
| AI Used | Always `Yes - Claude` |
| Basis | `ac` (only ACs read) / `plan` (only implementation read) / `both` |
| Manual TCs | Test cases **created or updated** with AI help this sprint |
| Automated TCs | Of those, how many became automated test cases |
| Reason | Why the remainder was not automated (required when automated < manual) |

## Honesty rules

- Count only what actually exists. Planned-but-not-written cases are not automated.
- Never invent a number to fill a cell. Leave it at 0 and say so.
- The `--reason` field is required whenever `automated < manual`.

## Where records are stored

`~/.config/qi-activity/<TICKET-KEY>.json` — one JSON file per ticket, on the local machine.
Records persist across sessions. The `report` command aggregates by sprint.
Set `QI_ACTIVITY_DIR` to store records elsewhere (used by the eval harness to isolate runs).
